## What changed

**`src/intervals.ts`** — implemented `mergeIntervals`:
- Validates every input pair up front; a pair whose `end < start` throws a `RangeError` that names the offending interval by index (e.g. `Invalid interval at index 1: [5, 3] ends below its start`). Because validation runs before any merging, an invalid pair anywhere in the list throws, even one that would have been absorbed by a merge.
- Sorts a *copy* of the outer array by `start`, then sweeps once, merging when `start <= last.end` (so both overlap and touch are covered), widening the running interval when needed.
- Never mutates the input: the outer array is only read (sorted via `[...intervals]`), the input pairs are only read, and the returned pairs are fresh arrays.

**`src/intervals.test.ts`** (new) — 14 tests via `bun:test`: empty input, single interval, sorting of disjoint intervals, overlap/touch merging in any order, chained touches, contained intervals, exact-end widening, negative/decimal bounds, zero-length intervals, no mutation of the input array or its order, fresh returned pairs, `RangeError` naming the index, and throwing even when a valid merge precedes the invalid pair.

